meta {
  name: Prompt Direct
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/llm/prompt?prompt=In one sentence, what is a Supertrend indicator?&model=qwen3:8b&think=false
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  prompt: In one sentence, what is a Supertrend indicator?
  model: qwen3:8b
  think: false
  ~timeout: 60
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # LLM Prompt Direct

  The simplest possible way to talk to the local LLM: send a prompt, get the raw
  text reply. No trading logic, no JSON contract, no multi-timeframe distillation
  — a thin passthrough for quick testing and prompt tinkering.

  ## Two forms
  - GET  /api/llm/prompt?prompt=...   — quick, prompt in the query string (this request)
  - POST /api/llm/prompt              — prompt in the request body (for longer text);
                                        same query params for model/think/timeout

  ## Query params
  - `prompt`  — the text to send (required; GET).
  - `model`   — model tag; omit to use app.llm.model (qwen3:8b). Use qwen3:14b for
                the deeper model.
  - `think`   — true enables the model's step-by-step reasoning monologue (slower);
                default false.
  - `timeout` — per-call timeout in seconds; omit to use app.llm.timeout-seconds.

  ## Response (200)
  { model, think, latencyMs, prompt, response, timestamp }

  ## Errors
  - `400` — empty prompt.
  - `503` — app.llm.enabled=false.
  - `502` — the runtime call failed (down/timeout); `detail` explains why.

  Requires app.llm.enabled=true and a reachable runtime with the model pulled.
  Testing only — nothing here trades.
}
